+Open http://localhost:3031, choose the spreadsheet and an environment, then choose what to check:
+
+- Risk API: every row sent to the service, from the server or from the browser, with a live tape of results.
+- Calculator form, headless browsers on the server: Playwright fills the form, each browser is streamed live to the page over a WebSocket (CDP screencast, typically 30-40 fps), and Playwright records one video per browser or one per row.
+- Calculator form, in this browser: the calculator loads in a frame on the page (its HTML is rebased so scripts and the risk API are the real ones) and is filled in with real DOM events in front of the viewer. The tab can be recorded with the browser's own screen capture, one video for the run or one per row; the recording stays on the viewer's machine.
+- ASC Audit form: as the headless calculator run, with sign-in by cookie header or username and password.
+- Load test: concurrent users against the risk API with every answer checked.
+
+Results show on screen and download as Excel, PDF (validation runs) or JSON. One headless form run at a time.
 
 `VALIDATION_WEB_PORT` and `VALIDATION_UI_DIR` configure the server. The Dockerfile builds on the Playwright image so form runs work in the container.
 
